Four bugs in HAUNTED multiplayer mode: border image only extended rightward, MP players couldn't use relics (server stored item name instead of ID breaking lookups), bots never received relics in MP, and inspecting another player's card didn't show their equipped skin.

## Changes

- **Border image (`PlayerStats.tsx`)**: Replaced asymmetric right-only extension (`left: 0, width: calc(100% + 96px)`) with symmetric `±12px` inset on all sides — border now covers all edges uniformly without `objectFit`

- **MP relic ID storage (`server/routes.ts`)**: `select_haunted_item` handler stored `data.itemName` but all `HAUNTED_ITEMS` lookups key on `r.id`. Changed to store `data.itemId`. Fixes both the USE RELIC button and the relic section in the player inspect dialog

- **Bot relic assignment (`server/gameEngine.ts`)**: Bots in MP HAUNTED mode never had `selectedItem` set — the bot activation loop at `startWaitingForReady` was a no-op. Now assigns random unique relics to bots in `confirmDriverInGame` after driver assignment, matching SP behavior

- **Cross-player skin inspection (`client/src/pages/Game.tsx`)**: Dialog `dialogSkinUrl` was gated to `isDialogCurrentPlayer && myCosmetics`. Other players' skins are now resolved from `selectedPlayerStats.equippedCosmetics` + `selectedPlayerStats.selectedDriver`, enabling skin passthrough inspection (e.g. accuser skin on BIO_FUEL accuser) for any player

```ts
// Before: skin only shown for own card
const dialogSkinUrl = isDialogCurrentPlayer && myCosmetics
  ? getDriverSkinUrl(myCosmetics, dialogDriverId) : null;

// After: use whichever player's cosmetics+driver is selected
const dialogCosmetics = isDialogCurrentPlayer ? myCosmetics : selectedPlayerStats?.equippedCosmetics;
const dialogSkinUrl = dialogCosmetics ? getDriverSkinUrl(dialogCosmetics, dialogDriverId) : null;
```

